      {
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "How is Zscaler different from other cloud security providers?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "<p>Zscaler is a 100% cloud-native platform built on zero trust principles. Unlike legacy vendors retrofitting old systems, Zscaler's architecture enables secure, direct-to-cloud connections&mdash;eliminating the need for VPNs, firewalls, and backhauling.&nbsp;</p>\n"
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "What should enterprises look for in a cloud security provider?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "<p>Key considerations include a zero trust architecture, global scalability, integrated threat protection, data loss prevention, and seamless support for hybrid and multi-cloud environments.&nbsp;</p>\n"
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "Can cloud enterprise security replace traditional firewalls and VPNs?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "<p>Yes. Modern cloud security platforms like Zscaler eliminate the need for legacy firewalls and VPNs by enforcing access and security policies in the cloud&mdash;closer to users and apps, not the data center.</p>\n"
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "How do cloud security providers support zero trust strategies?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "<p>Leading providers enable zero trust by verifying identity, device posture, and context before granting access to applications. Zscaler enforces these principles across all traffic&mdash;internal or external.&nbsp;</p>\n"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
